ity of  these leaked emails right Twitter said  well we don't discuss conversations with  possible or current advertisers but  nobody is denying the authenticity of  these leaked emails so why is this a big  right like why do we care why is it  important that Twitter can sell ads to  whoever they want why would we want to  bother with that a couple different  reasons no one is disputing Twitter's  right to sell ads to whoever they want  presuming that there's no other laws  that are being violated by those ad  sales the part where it gets interesting  is that just last week Twitter said  they're going to be banning all RT  related accounts from advertising on  Twitter a sort of proactive  organizational ban now why did Twitter  do that they said this decision was  based on the retrospective work we've  been doing around the 2016 election and  the US intelligence community's  conclusion that both RT and Sputnik  attempted to interfere with the election  on the behalf of the Russian government  the intelligence report in which Twitter  which Twitter reference called  RT the Kremlin's principle International  propaganda outlet so we need to cut  through the BS on this and very very  quickly there are people saying that it  was wrong for Twitter to ever offer ads  to RT and there are other people saying  it's wrong that now Twitter is banning  RT because it's a limitation on free  speech or censorship or something along  those lines  it's neither in a sense Twitter's  actions have actually been totally  consistent with the financial motive  before Twitter thought the best move is  let's try to get some Russian state  money they seem to want to buy election  ads let's try to get them to spend as  much money as possible on Twitter now  they thought let's try to clean up our  reputation by loudly saying we're not  going to allow RT to buy ads at all it's  the same thing in that sense twitter is  being completely consistent here it's  not about it being moral or immoral in 